            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CariSue"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Thank you, thank you, thank you for this recipe! I made a couple of changes after reading the reviews; vanilla instead of water, 2 egg whites and 1/2 white sugar and 1/2 brown sugar. My father loves pecans and I served this at his 60th birthday party. So many people asked me for this recipe I lost count after a while. Absolutely delicious and addiciting!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "anglwngs99"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are absolutely delicious. I've made them by the recipe and they are great. Having made them a few times I've made a few adjustments to suit my tastes. I use 1/2 white sugar and 1/2 brown sugar. After mixing the pecans with the sugar mixture in a plastic bag and spreading them out on my sheet pan, I sprinkle them with a little additional coarse salt. Can't beat the salty sweet combination!!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-23T12:11:26.887Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lori"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were soooo good. After reading the other reviews I used 2 egg whites, vanilla instead of water, brown sugar instead of white and added a pinch of cayenne. I also used a mix of pecans, almonds and cashews. I did use more nuts than called for and upped coating amts some to accommodate that and as such did follow one reviewers advice and baked them a little longer, 1 hr 20min as at 1 hour the coating just seemed to need a little more time yet. My husband went crazy over them.",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-17T17:07:52.957Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KendraDarigan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a HUGE hit! I took some liberties and added bacon though. I cooked thick cut bacon on the stove, chopped it up and tossed it with the pecans once they were done. I used an equal amount of bacon and pecans, but I'm sure it is easily adjusted. This will be served at all of my future parties!",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-06T08:58:33.280Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Strawberry Banana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is absolutely delicious. My dad loves these. My family isn't too big of a fan on cinnamon, so using only 1 teaspoon of cinnamon works too. Also, if you like honey toasted pecans, then use this recipe, but substitute the egg and water for 1/3 cup of honey. They are delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2018-01-19T23:20:28.333Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jamie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this recipe to make pecans for a fruit salad (lettuce, craisins, apples, grapes, pecans, and a raspberry dressing) with the following changes: replaced the water with vanilla extract, omitted the cinnamon, and halved the sugar. They worked great with my salad without being too sweet!",
            "datePublished": "2010-06-28T16:16:18.697Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Renee Schultz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have now made it 4 times to perfect it in my opinion and these are my recommendations from the original recipe:\nDefinitely replace the water with Vanilla\nDefinitely use 1/2 sugar and 1/2 brown sugar \nDo Not over heat the oven. If you want crispier nuts, use a 250 degree oven, for less crispy use 225.\nStir for sure every 15 minutes.\nEverything else was fine and these are addictive! Enjoy!",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-05T02:01:03.530Z"
          },
          {
